{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790888589,"nonce":"qCEMK/YOwDEeb+1LEnPxvPqFgjw=","title":"An Incident cannot be investigated as a whole, so a forty-Case storm would cost forty Investigations","message":"**What is wrong.** ADR 0053 §4: subjects include `incident`; triggers are drawn, membership change (coalesced), human request; a Case already in an Incident gets no automatic Investigation of its own; new Findings go outbound as facts. `enrichments_subjkind_ck` admits `alert`, `case`, `group` (`db/migrations/00069_a_conversation_is_a_case.sql:640`), so an Incident's Finding cannot be stored as an Enrichment at all.\n\n**The demonstration.** `180a525` investigates Cases only; an Enrichment row with `subject_kind='incident'` violates the CHECK.\n\n**Why it matters.** The cost and coherence argument for Incidents in the first place.\n\n**Where.** Investigation subject kind; `enrichments_subjkind_ck` widened to admit `incident` (and its Go copy); trigger wiring from the Incident domain using `bf172fe`'s minimum interval; Incident detail page; a \"new Finding\" reason in `aa6d18b`'s vocabulary.\n\n**Scope.** medium.\n\n**Done when.** Drawing an Incident starts one Investigation; membership churn inside the minimum interval yields one more; member Cases start none automatically; a Case's pre-existing Finding is readable by the Incident's Investigation; the latest Finding is stored as an `incident` Enrichment, shows on the Incident and goes outbound; going quiet triggers nothing.\n\n**Blocked by.** `180a525`, `bf172fe`, `61eeddf`, `aa6d18b`\n\n**Mode.** AFK — can be implemented and merged without a human decision. Source: ADR 0052/0053/0054 design session, 2026-10-02.","files":null}]}